{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions","id":625909,"title":"Werewolf Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T14:22:18-07:00","id":625909,"title":"Werewolf Devotions","content":"So Devotions are pretty cool. We all know it. Vampires get all the fun, don\u2019t they? Anyway, reading a couple threads on custom Devotions over in the Requiem section today got me thinking about something similar for Forsaken. I know this has been mentioned before but I can\u2019t recall any attempts at homebrew.<br /> <br /> My biggest problem is that I can\u2019t decide how this would be done. Should it be done simply through combining facets to create an all new effect? Or decoupling a facet from a specific renown and running its essence through multiple brands. Something else? Both? Right now I sort have it reflected both ways in my write ups, but I\u2019m worried the method dilute the simplicity and clarity of the gift system. Anyway, this is all very rough right now, so any suggestions, additions or any other kind of feedback is welcome and appreciated. Here\u2019s what I have so far: <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Devotions</b></span><br /> <br /> Whether through dedication, experimentation or raw, instinctive talent, exceptionally clever Uratha have been known to alter and combine facets to fit their needs, channeling their essence through multiple channels to create new and unique effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaze of Glorious Lunacy</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Glorious Lunacy, Gaze of the Moon, Wisdom 2</i><br /> <br /> The Uratha's eyes flicker bright gold for a moment as she draws the Moon\u2019s bright madness into her gaze, triggering something primal in her prey.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> When using this Facet, the Uratha targets up his Glory renown in humans he can clearly see. The prey are subjected to Awestruck condition as if the Uratha was in Gauru form and had activated the Glorious Lunacy facet.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaze of Raging Lunacy</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Raging Lunacy, Gaze of the Moon, Wisdom 2</i><br /> <br /> The Uratha's eyes flicker deep red for a moment as he draws the Moon\u2019s bright madness into his gaze, triggering something primal in his prey.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> When using this Facet, the Uratha targets up to her Glory renown in humans she can clearly see. The prey are subjected to Berserk condition as if the Uratha was in Gauru form and had activated the Raging Lunacy facet.<br /> <br /> <b>King of the Hill</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Lay Low the Challenger, Perfected Rage, Honor 3.</i><br /> <br /> There can be only one true apex predator, even an Uratha in the throes of rage must yield to this principle.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <br /> This facet may only be activated in Garou form and after the <b>Perfected Rage</b> facet has been activated. Upon striking an Uratha in Garou form, The Uratha may add the positive difference between their respective Honor renown to the number of turns he can maintain the form. His opponent also loses the negative difference in which he can maintain his own rage. If the Uratha\u2019s Honor renown is less than his opponent\u2019s, then the effect is reversed.<br /> When striking an opponent in Kuruth, the Uratha instead gains twice this difference in turns to maintain the form. May only be used once per scene per opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Martyr</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Memento Mori, Berserker's Might, Honor 3, Glory 3</i><br /> <br /> Fluff fluff. You probably don\u2019t expect to survive. Packmates feel pain, but the wounds leave no mark? Fluff fluff.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Essence per turn<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Stamina + Occult + Honor<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Uratha cannot cancel this gift or its sympathetic link until she runs out of essence or dies. If the Uratha dies, all the total damage she has accrued is received by each packmate, as the sudden severance of the link creates a violent feedback.<br /> <b>Success:</b> All damage that the Uratha\u2019s packmates receive is transferred to the facet user (reduced by her Glory renown + the activation roll). Any aggravated damage received through this gift bypasses the damage reduction and is doubled, as the Uratha\u2019s sympathetic link with her pack amplifies her pain.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Aggravated damage still bypasses damage reduction, but is not doubled.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 08-14-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T14:28:16-07:00","id":625935,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some notes for myself: </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Considering making </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">King of the Hill</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> run through Glory as opposed to Honor (in line with the idea of channeling a facet through multiple spirit brands). Also maybe looking for a gender neutral name for it, haha.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m still tinkering with </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Glorious Martyr</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Maybe have it last for Honor renown in turns as opposed to the Crimson Spasm essence model.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also considering a Stamina + Resolve roll each turn with a cumulative penalty. Or maybe whenever the Uratha suffers wound penalties.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also considering not doubling aggravated damage at all, and having the exceptional success condition instead make it so that aggravated damage does not bypass the damage reduction.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also toying around with the idea that Uratha shouldn't able to teach Devotions because of how complex it is to manipulate facets this way, the method being unique to each Uratha's unique spirit and physiology.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another idea is that using multiple devotions per scene can lead to the Essence Overload condition. Or perhaps an Essence Jam. Like getting food down the wrong pipe. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also maybe a limit of 1 devotion per primal urge? Since that's what governs essence use. Just trying to find ways to limit devotions, but maybe the prerequisites are enough?</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:28:12-07:00","id":625989,"title":"","content":"They sort of have it in fetishes, one of their powers being able to make, 'a modification to a specific Facet that allows it to be used in new ways.'<br /> <br /> An example is the Gridlock Puzzle, which alters the facet All Doors Locked. All Doors Locked allows the werewolf to have complete control of all the 'doors, windows and other entryways in a building or vehicle the Uratha is touching or is inside.' This control contains awareness, as well, letting the werewolf know where they are, if they're open or closed, and said werewolf can lock them or open them with a thought.<br /> <br /> The Gridlock Puzzle opens this facet up to the streets. 'Rather than doors and windows, the Uratha can instead control all traffic lights and other forms of traffic control...'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:34:37-07:00","id":625997,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. How does that work, anyway? Like, is there any detail on the interaction between the werewolf's spirit and the fetish in the case of modified facets?<br /> <br /> I still like the idea of combining facets as opposed to just altering one, though - but it would be easy enough to modify any of these devotions I listed to just be variants on one of the facets. I would probably have to modify the power level of some of them, though, but pretty simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:37:30-07:00","id":626001,"title":"","content":"Ok.. the two Gaze enhancers... All that they really do is lower the Essence cost by 1. I don't think it's worth paying XP for that.<br /> <br /> King of the Hill is a pretty neat one, but potentially game-breaking, as it allows indefinite Gauru when fighting non-werewolves.<br /> <br /> And for the last one? Umm, I suppose it has it's place.. But giving the entire pack an additional 4+ Damage reduction in addition to throwing it to someone else is... I dunno, a little too good?<br /> Combined with that it takes an action to use it, and it costs a lot, it's theoretically balanced out, but... The combination of strong damage-reduction, and transfer is simply too good. Activate this one and go Gauru, and silver is the only way to take down any member of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:39:55-07:00","id":626004,"title":"","content":"A werewolf normally pushes their Essence through their Gift's Mark and it exits out their Renown brand. Presumably the inclusion of the spirit bound in the fetish adds another element to it, filtering the werewolf's Essence through the spirit first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:43:27-07:00","id":626007,"title":"","content":"&quot;Upon striking an opponent who is also in Garou form&quot; is what that means. I'll edit for clarity. So King of the Hill would can only be used when striking another Garou, and even then only on once per opponent.<br /> <br /> As far as the Glorious Martyr, I'll specify that it can't be used in Garou as the rage interferes with maintaining a sympathetic link.<br /> <br /> You're right about the gaze ones, I'll think about that and modify or scrap them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:20:04-07:00","id":626440,"title":"","content":"I 've been thinking of something similar through gift of the elementals something as berserkers might + the earth facet allowing to downgrade damage in addition to the damage reduction , or slaughterer + tongue of fire for increased fire damage or hit and run + wind for enhanced movement. The dame could be achieved through fetishes, but I do like the idea of uratha honingvtheir skills and aplying ceativity to better exploit their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T03:18:35-07:00","id":626469,"title":"","content":"This sounds like something that would make more sense when applied to Wolf Gifts than Shadow or Moon ones, given as the latter two are modifications to the uratha made by spirits. Wolf Gifts, on the other hand, are entirely the werewolves' own, and thus far more receptive to personal experimentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T04:05:49-07:00","id":626478,"title":"","content":"I considered the possibility to have Milestone facets once you have all facets to create new effects. But this idea of &quot;Devotions&quot; is cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:22:01-07:00","id":626728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=626001#post626001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok.. the two Gaze enhancers... All that they really do is lower the Essence cost by 1. I don't think it's worth paying XP for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Common misconception: Per RAW, the fetish merit is only something you pay for (with experience) at character creation. It's not something like &quot;This elder gave me this magic sword because I saved his life. I have 4 less experience for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> That would be like charging XP for a +4 sword in D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 08-14-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T11:51:09-07:00","id":626761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=626728#post626728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Common misconception: Per RAW, the fetish merit is only something you pay for (with experience) at character creation. It's not something like &amp;quot;This elder gave me this magic sword because I saved his life. I have 4 less experience for it.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That would be like charging XP for a +4 sword in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking about 1st edition? Cause in 2e there isn't even a Fetish Merit, you have to craft or obtain them during play, or talk to your ST if you want to start out with one or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:39:42-07:00","id":626826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=626478#post626478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered the possibility to have Milestone facets once you have all facets to create new effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:19:55-07:00","id":626967,"title":"","content":"I could see something along these lines as sort of emergent patterns---advantages that crop up should any werewolf meet all the prerequisites. Those would generally be combinations or upgrades on the extant powers, I'm thinking. Given the spiritual links, perhaps these things should only appear when one accomplishes some spiritual feat that earns it. Unless the gift involves the essence of study in some way, I don't see research as being relevant to acquisition.<br /> <br /> You could also have some gifts that spirits won't (or even literally can't) teach a lesser werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T00:51:30-07:00","id":627359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=626728#post626728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Common misconception: Per RAW, the fetish merit is only something you pay for (with experience) at character creation. It's not something like &quot;This elder gave me this magic sword because I saved his life. I have 4 less experience for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> That would be like charging XP for a +4 sword in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse me.. but what are you talking about? I don't understand what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T05:53:31-07:00","id":628486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=627359#post627359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excuse me.. but what are you talking about? I don't understand what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephsy meant that Fetishes earned through gameplay do not cost experience. But as Charlaquin noted, in 2nd edition Fetishes never cost XP, even when you start with them because of background reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T01:00:18-07:00","id":629679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=628486#post628486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ephsy meant that Fetishes earned through gameplay do not cost experience. But as Charlaquin noted, in 2nd edition Fetishes never cost XP, even when you start with them because of background reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... But I don't get where Fetishes came into it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T02:58:39-07:00","id":629774,"title":"","content":"The argument was that they're basically the werewolf equivalent of devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T03:48:53-07:00","id":629786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=629774#post629774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument was that they're basically the werewolf equivalent of devotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Myeah. But OP seemed to just want regular Devotions, just for Werewolves. And I said I wouldn't pay XP for two of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:26:21-07:00","id":630711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/625909-werewolf-devotions?p=626469#post626469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like something that would make more sense when applied to Wolf Gifts than Shadow or Moon ones, given as the latter two are modifications to the uratha made by spirits. Wolf Gifts, on the other hand, are entirely the werewolves' own, and thus far more receptive to personal experimentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Elfive. Werewolf devotions would make more sense with wolf gifts than shadow gifts. It is the werewolf's natural ability and power, unlike shadow gifts. <br /> <br /> To be honest I always wanted to try something like this for werewolf but I didn't know how exactly. W:tF is my favorite game line of all the others and I felt a little envious of vampire and mage being able to combine their abilities/powers to make new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T23:27:03-07:00","id":630737,"title":"","content":"I actually don't see much of a point for Devotions to exist with Werewolf's Gift structure as it exist now.<br /> <br /> Rather, I think the purpose of them would be best served by creating a Gift that is based on two other gifts (which are the Prerequisites to getting this Gift) and then making facets out of it... or just skipping Prerequisites all together and having them as normal gifts.<br /> <br /> Werewolf's Gift structure is designed to be... massively flexible despite offering single powers to the point that adding Devotions on top might be a downgrade or be too expensive (assuming you are giving them an exp cost like vamp Devotions). I feel that the only real...Devotions might well be &quot;Mastery&quot; Gifts that are earned by completing an entire List.<br /> <br /> However, I will state I would like King of the Hill on my characters. Though I think it maybe it should maybe treat the user as having +1 or +2 for the purposes of determining Renown difference. Only because to make it so that Werewolves who take the pains to learn it aren't completely wasting their Essence when fighting equally matched foes and could stand a chance against slightly better foes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 08-18-2015, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:41:03-07:00","id":631016,"title":"","content":"I never really read the Wolf Gift lists as exhaustive anyway. I mean, even the Gifts themselves are just loose categories of powers. There's no key needed to unlock them and so you could shuffle the facets in them around without much trouble. Maw of Madness looks a bit shoehorned into Pack Gifts, for example. I would totally accept that as being what happened in-universe. So the idea that a werewolf could just discover new ones isn't too far out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}